<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysian forex market closed for festivals.</title>
<headline>Malaysian forex market closed for festivals.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The foreign exchange market in Malaysia was closed on Friday for the Chinese Lunar New Year.</p>
<p>The country's banking institutions will remain closed until Tuesday, February 11, for a twin celebration, which includes the Moslem Eid al-Fitr.</p>
<p>The ringgit was last quoted at 2.4925/45 a dollar from Melbourne on Friday morning.</p>
<p>The ringgit is expected to trade in a wide 2.48-2.50 a dollar range in the near-term.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
